   - The mean of the exponential distribution is \(\mu = 3\).
   - The standard deviation of the exponential distribution is \(\sigma = 3\).
   - The sample size is \(n = 36\).
   - The mean of \(\bar{X}\) is \(\mu_{\bar{X}} = \mu = 3\).
   - The standard error (standard deviation of \(\bar{X}\)) is \(\sigma_{\bar{X}} = \frac{\sigma}{\sqrt{n}} = \frac{3}{6} = 0.5\).

2. **Convert the sample mean limits to z-scores:**
   - For the lower bound \(2.5\):
     \[
     z_{\text{lower}} = \frac{2.5 - 3}{0.5} = \frac{-0.5}{0.5} = -1
     \]
   - For the upper bound \(4\):
     \[
     z_{\text{upper}} = \frac{4 - 3}{0.5} = \frac{1}{0.5} = 2
     \]

